From: hIRoic Linux hammer PoC <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: mmci: add peripheral flow-controller option

STM32F746 SDMMC is capable of terminating a DMA transfer as the peripheral
flow controller.  The STM32CubeF7 board driver enables DMA PFCTRL for both
receive and transmit, but generic MMCI hard-codes device_fc=false.  With the
DMA controller in charge, a one-sector receive completes while words remain
in the MMCI FIFO; MMCI consequently declares the DMA buggy and falls back to
PIO.

Add an ST-specific opt-in property and pass it through dma_slave_config.  It
is deliberately disabled by default so the behavior of all existing MMCI
users remains unchanged.

Upstream-status: Not submitted [STM32F746 board validation]
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/mmc/arm,pl18x.yaml         | 5 +++++
 drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c                            | 4 +++-
 drivers/mmc/host/mmci.h                            | 1 +
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/arm,pl18x.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/arm,pl18x.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/arm,pl18x.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/arm,pl18x.yaml
@@ -116,6 +116,11 @@ properties:
     description: ST Micro-specific property, use CKIN pin from an external
       driver to sample the receive data (for example with a voltage switch
       transceiver).
+
+  st,dma-peripheral-flow-controller:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/flag
+    description: ST Micro-specific property, let the MMCI peripheral control
+      the number of data items transferred by the external DMA controller.
 
   st,cmd-gpios:
     maxItems: 1
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c b/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.c
@@ -944,8 +944,8 @@ static int _mmci_dmae_prep_data(struct mmci_host *host, struct mmc_data *data,
 		.src_addr_width = DMA_SLAVE_BUSWIDTH_4_BYTES,
 		.dst_addr_width = DMA_SLAVE_BUSWIDTH_4_BYTES,
 		.src_maxburst = variant->fifohalfsize >> 2, /* # of words */
 		.dst_maxburst = variant->fifohalfsize >> 2, /* # of words */
-		.device_fc = false,
+		.device_fc = host->dma_peripheral_fc,
 	};
 	struct dma_chan *chan;
 	struct dma_device *device;
@@ -2049,6 +2049,8 @@ static int mmci_of_parse(struct device_node *np, struct mmc_host *mmc)
 		host->clk_reg_add |= MCI_STM32_CLK_NEGEDGE;
 	if (of_get_property(np, "st,use-ckin", NULL))
 		mmci_probe_level_translator(mmc);
+	if (of_property_read_bool(np, "st,dma-peripheral-flow-controller"))
+		host->dma_peripheral_fc = true;
 
 	if (of_get_property(np, "mmc-cap-mmc-highspeed", NULL))
 		mmc->caps |= MMC_CAP_MMC_HIGHSPEED;
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.h b/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.h
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.h
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/mmci.h
@@ -436,6 +436,7 @@ struct mmci_host {
 
 	u8			use_dma:1;
 	u8			dma_in_progress:1;
+	u8			dma_peripheral_fc:1;
 	void			*dma_priv;
 
 	s32			next_cookie;
-- 
